  "method": [
    "Before scoring, independently reconstruct the 25 fixed grid lags plus all prior cutoffs for the exact 49 previously confirmed corridor-incident pairs. Verify complete confirmed/rejected accounting and exact previously reviewed scope signatures.",
    "Verify hashes, unchanged original provenance/configuration, all 322 original prediction records, all retained modes/candidates, selected trains and baseline timestamps against retained as-of inputs, and exact active notice versions against latest raw alert captures.",
    "After scoring, independently reconstruct all selected-journey endpoint usability, catchability, walking/waiting/riding totals, failure reasons, cross-policy comparisons and report aggregates from original label sources.",
    "Compare raw-MTA strict recommended journey in raw-MTA mode against the incident-profile strict recommended journey in incident-profile mode; do not substitute the fastest raw-MTA candidate or the model-mode Stay journey.",
    "Verify all 322 original full-mode scored records remain identical. Preserve the complete frozen result and separately audit the five comparable incremental cases against raw journals."
  ],
  "conclusions": [
    "There are 13 strict raw-MTA Stay to incident-profile Switch checkpoints across nine corridor-incident pairs and 11 distinct incident/train-sequence pairs.",
    "Three checkpoints across three incident families show fixed-selected-train proxy savings greater than 180 seconds; two are practical ties and eight have unknown complete gains.",
    "Two meaningful Grand Central 5-to-4 substitutions have near-event endpoint evidence and no earlier known usable exact-line 5 in the bounded diagnostic. Same-station substitution is a valid Switch under the user-approved policy.",
    "Court Square's 82m50s fixed-run gain does not establish savings against an adaptive passenger staying on the 7; earlier near-event 7 trains exist.",
    "The available records do not supply five to ten independently supported meaningful incremental wins under this exact rule."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The test week and original results were already known; this is a separate post-hoc systematic supplement, not an untouched evaluation.",
    "Checkpoints repeat incidents and sometimes the same train sequence; counts are not independent passenger-level success rates.",
    "Final MTA predictions plus configured walks are screened outcome proxies, not independent passenger observations.",
    "Near-event label support and feasible arithmetic do not validate actual pedestrian access time or guarantee catching a train with little slack.",
    "Unknown or missed-selected-train outcomes are never converted into successes.",
    "Bounded earlier-same-line searches do not establish archive completeness or a fully simulated adaptive Stay policy.",
    "The matched-policy aggregate includes one 626-second model benefit whose Stay departure label persists for 971 seconds after its timestamp; the arrival endpoint is near-event. This additional proxy-quality caveat does not affect the 33 comparable model-Switch-versus-Stay pairs or the five comparable raw-Stay/model-Switch disagreements. The frozen aggregate is not silently reclassified."
  ],
